OL,3,GNEWSACancer care time of day 'could
OL,4,Ainfluence outcomes'
OL,5,
OL,6,FResearchers have found that the time of
OL,7,Fday at which cancer patients get their
OL,8,Ftreatment could have a significant
OL,9,Feffect on survival rates.
OL,11,FPatients who had morning immunotherapy
OL,12,Fsessions lived longer than those
OL,13,Ftreated in the afternoon, the research
OL,14,Fsuggested.
OL,16,FCancer specialists at the University of
OL,17,FSouthampton and Cardiff University are
OL,18,Fexpected to carry out randomised trials
OL,19,Fto confirm the hypothesis.
OL,23,APub: 01-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,337,330,200,160,0,100
